# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Belt-and-braces against committing credentials from ANY repo, not
# just ones with a good .gitignore. `.env.example` / `.env.sample` are
# re-included: CLAUDE.md calls them safe (placeholders, no real values)
# and they're meant to be committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cert
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
credentials/

# ── Logs and local caches ────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: a global *.log rule hides log files in EVERY repo, including a
# project that legitimately tracks one (fixtures, golden output). To
# re-include per repo, add a negation to that repo's .gitignore:
#     !tests/fixtures/expected.log
# or force it once with `git add -f path/to.log`.
# `git ignored` lists everything currently hidden this way.
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
__pycache__/
.venv/